hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"357","Abu Musa Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, Al-Dahhak bin Mukhlid told us, Sufyan told us, Abdullah bin Abi Bakr told me, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Shall I not inform you of what God expiates sins with? And He increases in good deeds?” They said: Yes, O Messenger of God. He said: “Performing ablution thoroughly in times of hardship, and waiting for prayer after prayer. None of you is a man who He leaves his house and prays with the imam, then sits and waits for the next prayer, except for the angels, saying: O God, forgive him, O God, have mercy on him.” . Then he mentioned the hadith. Abu Bakr said: No one narrated this except Abu Asim."
"358","Bundar told us, Yahya told us, Ubayd Allah bin Umar told us, Khubayb bin Abdul Rahman told me, on the authority of Hafs bin Asim, on the authority of Abu Hurairah. On the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “There are seven whom God will shade under His shade on the Day when there will be no shade but His shade: the just Imam, and a young man who grew up in worship.” God, and a man whose heart was devoted to the mosques, and two men who loved each other for the sake of God, uniting for the sake of God and separating for him, and a man who was sought by a woman in a high position. And Jamal, and he said: I fear God, and a man who gave charity in secret, whose right hand does not know what his left can do, and a man who mentioned God in private and it overflowed. \His eyes.\"" Pindar once told us: A woman of dignity and beauty"," and he said: I am. Abu Bakr said: This is the expression"," “His right hand does not know what to spend with his left","” in which he contradicted Yahya bin Saeed"," and said: Who narrated this? The news is other than Yahya"," his left hand does not know what his right hand can do."""
"359","It is narrated by Bundar, it is narrated by Yahya bin Saeed, it is narrated by Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Saeed bin Abi Saeed, on the authority of Saeed bin Yasar, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “There is no man who used to visit the mosques and was distracted by a matter or illness, then returned to the way he was, but he rejoices in God’s glory.” To Him just as the family of an absent person rejoices in their absence when he comes.”"
